Do not advertise the X910 SSC ambient-light sensor to desktop clients.

The Samsung firmware discovers the stk31610 and accepts its enable request but
never sends the configuration response which completes
ssc_sensor_light_open_sync().  libssc 0.4.4 waits for synchronous completion by
spinning the default GLib context without blocking, so GNOME's automatic-light
claim pins iio-sensor-proxy at one full CPU and aggravates the ADSP handover IRQ
storm.  The sensor also reports a constant zero lux on this board, so exposing
it provides no usable feature.

Keep accelerometer and compass through SSC, and leave automatic brightness
disabled until the light request protocol is understood.

diff --git a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
index a7dba30..bf3efb1 100644
--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
@@ -81,7 +81,6 @@ static const SensorDriver * const drivers[] = {
 	&input_proximity,
 #ifdef HAS_LIBSSC
 	&ssc_proximity,
-	&ssc_light,
 	&ssc_accel,
 	&ssc_compass,
 #endif
